  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 20-layer planar multilayer filter on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: MgF2, HfO2, MgF2, HfO2, MgF2, HfO2, MgF2, HfO2, MgF2, HfO2, MgF2, HfO2, MgF2, HfO2, MgF2, HfO2, MgF2, HfO2, MgF2, HfO2 (20 finite layers total). Each layer thickness bounded between 20 nm and 200 nm. Initialize thicknesses at quarter-wave optical depth centered on 267.5 nm wavelength (MgF2 n≈1.38, HfO2 n≈2.0 at UV). Use coherent S-matrix solver across 255-1100 nm spectrum. Score three transmittance objectives: maximize mean transmittance 255-280 nm, minimize mean transmittance 300-700 nm, minimize mean transmittance 700-1100 nm. Use bound-aware global optimizer with projection of out-of-bounds samples back into feasible region. Normal incidence, unpolarized light. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 255-280 nm, 300-700 nm, 700-1100 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance in 255–280 nm; low transmittance in 300–700 nm; low transmittance in 700–1100 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 300–700 nm; transmittance in 700–1100 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30; no metal layers; conventional depositable inorganic dielectric materials only.",
